From 240de30227606ee8a37d4eaa1d83ba37fa2eff99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: renzbagaporo <renz.bagaporo@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 08:57:10 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: modem: cellular: attach chat before redial on
 registered

Entering RUN_DIAL_SCRIPT from DORMANT releases the chat and arms a 0 ms
timer, whose TIMEOUT attaches the chat to DLCI1 and runs the dial
script. A REGISTERED event handled before that timer runs, such as one
parsed from a +CEREG URC queued behind the PPP_DEAD that left DORMANT,
cancels the timer and runs the dial script on the released chat. That
returns -EPERM unchecked, nothing is left armed, and the driver stays
in RUN_DIAL_SCRIPT without dialing until it is suspended.

Reschedule the timeout instead, so the dial always goes through the
TIMEOUT path that attaches the chat first. When the chat is already
attached this only moves a pending retry forward, as before.

Signed-off-by: renzbagaporo <renz.bagaporo@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/modem/modem_cellular.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/modem/modem_cellular.c b/drivers/modem/modem_cellular.c
index de2fcf73380..f740db00b24 100644
--- a/drivers/modem/modem_cellular.c
+++ b/drivers/modem/modem_cellular.c
@@ -1279,10 +1279,13 @@ static void modem_cellular_run_dial_script_event_handler(struct modem_cellular_d
 		modem_pipe_open_async(data->uart_pipe);
 		break;
 	case MODEM_CELLULAR_EVENT_REGISTERED:
-		/* Restart immediately, if we are waiting to retry the dial-script */
+		/* Restart immediately, if we are waiting to retry the dial-script.
+		 * The timeout attaches the chat before running the script: on
+		 * entry from dormant the chat was just released, and running the
+		 * script here would fail with no timer left to retry it.
+		 */
 		if (!modem_chat_is_running(&data->chat)) {
-			modem_cellular_stop_timer(data);
-			modem_chat_run_script_async(&data->chat, config->dial_chat_script);
+			k_work_reschedule(&data->timeout_work, K_NO_WAIT);
 		}
 		break;
 	default:
